    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0589" n="467" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg467"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herbert to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-24"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 24, 1888</date>.
                        (Received November 26.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of yesterday’s
                    date, asking for an early settlement of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bridgewater</hi> case, I have the honor to inform you that I telegraphed to
                    Her Majesty’s principal secretary of state <pb facs="0590" n="468"
                        xml:id="pg468"/> for foreign affairs, in the sense of your above-mentioned
                    note, and have received a reply stating that the owner of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bridgewater</hi>, before presenting the claim, commenced
                    an action at law which is still pending, and that the Canadian Government is
                    unable to express an opinion on the claim until the settlement of the case in
                    the law courts.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur Herbert.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
